1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,700
At dawn, Lake Tana wakes in silence.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:06,940
Ethiopia's largest lake, the source of
the Blue Nile.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:12,226
For ages, tankwa paddlers have travelled
through this water.

4
00:00:12,226 --> 00:00:14,523
The lake is their road and their home.

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,085
But hidden in the island forests are
ancient

6
00:00:19,085 --> 00:00:21,739
monasteries with a history older than
the lake.

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,710
On their walls, saints appear in richly
coloured paintings.

8
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:31,844
Every painting is both a prayer and a
lesson.

9
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,527
Books written on parchment have kept
ancient

10
00:00:35,527 --> 00:00:37,507
knowledge and faith alive for centuries.

11
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:44,769
By candlelight, scribes wrote word by
word, page by page.

12
00:00:44,769 --> 00:00:46,929
Their patience is still clear today.

13
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:54,607
In times of war and hardship, these
treasures were kept safe on the islands.

14
00:00:54,607 --> 00:00:56,344
The waves could not erase them.

15
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:01,238
Today this trust is in our hands.

16
00:01:01,238 --> 00:01:04,042
To know it, honour it and protect it is
our part.

17
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:08,872
Tana is not only a beautiful lake.

18
00:01:08,872 --> 00:01:10,663
It is a story the waves could not erase,

19
00:01:10,663 --> 00:01:12,678
so let us protect it for the next
generation.
